60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The firm’s terms require someone to be present and tidy beforehand. That means the time burden isn’t removed, just shifted. I cannot accept a system that leaves me with the same hours.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, I hear you, but the calendar proves we can’t all be here. A rota lets us skip when we’re away, which is fairer than permanent ownership.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, a rota forces constant coordination. The previous tenants’ silence came from rigid, permanent boundaries. I fear a fixed schedule creates the same isolation, just with more paperwork.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
